# Reviewed exceptions to the pre-publication audit.
#
# Format:  <path-prefix>  <rule-keyword>  # <reason>
#
# BOTH fields are required. A path-only waiver would hide every other rule on
# that path — which is exactly how a waiver added here for loopback addresses
# also buried leftover coursework wording in docs/ until it was caught by hand.
# Waived hits are still printed by the audit; they only stop blocking.
#
# This client deliberately manages a local agent in Docker, so the loopback
# address is part of the product rather than a leftover development endpoint.
# Binding to loopback IS the security property: the local agent must not be
# reachable from other machines.

Dockerfile                      endpoint  # Healthcheck probes its own loopback port.
docker-compose.yml              endpoint  # Publishes the agent to loopback only.
docker-compose.integration.yml  endpoint  # Same, for the integration stack.
tests/                          endpoint  # Python tests bind ephemeral loopback ports and
                                          # assert the compose file publishes to loopback.
ConnectOnionMacClientTests/     endpoint  # Swift tests feed loopback URLs into address
                                          # normalisation and rejection paths.
docs/                           endpoint  # Documentation shows the endpoint users curl.
README.md                       endpoint  # The Configure table documents the local port.
ViewModels/AgentTypes.swift     endpoint  # The one built-in discovery target, inside
                                          # `#if DEBUG`. Release builds compile an empty
                                          # list — see automaticDiscoveryTargets.
ViewModels/ViewModels.swift     endpoint  # Rejects loopback hosts when validating a
                                          # user-entered address; the literals are the
                                          # denylist itself.
